===BODY===
          <h2>Breaking down on the Autobahn</h2>
          <p>If you break down on a German Autobahn, get onto the hard shoulder, switch on your hazard lights, put on your reflective vest and wait behind the barrier. Emergency phones along the Autobahn connect you to help, and 112 works for emergencies. A local recovery service will usually take the car to a garage or storage yard first. That's where we collect it from.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from anywhere in Germany. Many of our German collections are in the west, around Cologne, Düsseldorf, Aachen and the Ruhr, which is the closest part of Germany to the Channel. But we also collect from Frankfurt, Stuttgart, Munich, Hamburg, Berlin and everywhere in between.</p>

          <h2>How the car comes back</h2>
          <p>From western Germany, the route home usually runs through Belgium and France to the Channel, or via the ferry ports in the Netherlands. We choose the most efficient route and quote one fixed price for the whole trip, collection to delivery.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Environmental zones:</strong> many German cities have Umweltzonen that need a green sticker, including for UK cars. They don't affect us collecting a broken-down car, but they matter if you plan to drive on.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Insurance</h2>
          <p>Check whether your European breakdown cover includes repatriation. If you need to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote you can send to your insurer.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you collect my car from a German garage?
A: Yes. Send us the garage name and address, make sure any fees are settled, and tell the garage we'll be collecting the car.
Q: How long does it take to bring a car back from Germany?
A: From western Germany it can be fairly quick. From the south or east it takes longer. We'll give you an estimate with the quote.
Q: Can you bring back a van?
A: Yes. We repatriate vans and light commercial vehicles too. Tell us the size and whether it's loaded.
